      "math_academy_id": "e-3179",
      "problem": "What is the circumference $C$ of a circle with a radius of $6?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14183030/assets/3c21021529285f488ca794a442e5826a033ed2a4c6f4fad53ab9e8fdc84d35ee.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
